<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Josip Broz Tito</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1892–1980</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tito</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Josip Broz Tito led the Communist Partisans against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>, setting up his first headquarters at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzice">Užice</a> in 1941. He ruled socialist Yugoslavia from 1945 until his death, broke with Stalin in 1948, developed workers' self-management and helped found the Non-Aligned Movement. The federation he held together broke up a decade after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/josip-broz-tito.jpg" alt="Josip Broz Tito" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Josip_Broz_Tito_uniform_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
